# Docker build context is the repo root (compose `build.context: ..`,
# docs/specs/07-docker.md §3.3). node_modules/.output must stay out of the
# context — they would bloat the transfer and break layer caching — and
# .env files must never reach an image (localhost addresses inside would
# shadow the compose wiring; `dotenv` only fills unset vars, so this is a
# hygiene guarantee, not a correctness one).

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.output
**/.nuxt
**/dist
**/coverage
**/src/generated
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# local env / dev secrets — compose env + docker secrets are the only source
**/.env
**/.env.*
infra/secrets

.git
docs

# The context DOES need infra/docker/ (Dockerfile.service COPYs
# infra/docker/entrypoint.sh) — so `infra` is NOT ignored wholesale, only
# the pieces Docker never consumes.
infra/postgres
